    {
      "id": "q_triads-ch4-checkpoint.where-the-fifth-sits",
      "kind": "choice",
      "prompt": [
        {
          "text": "C major, second inversion, on strings 2-3-4 is "
        },
        {
          "text": "x x 5 5 5 x",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " — "
        },
        {
          "text": "G",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " "
        },
        {
          "text": "C",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " "
        },
        {
          "text": "E",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", low to high. Which note is the fifth, and where does it go to make the chord augmented?"
        }
      ],
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "a",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "The bass note, up one fret — "
            },
            {
              "text": "x x 6 5 5 x",
              "marks": ["code"]
            },
            {
              "text": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "The top note, up one fret — "
            },
            {
              "text": "x x 5 5 6 x",
              "marks": ["code"]
            },
            {
              "text": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "The middle note, up one fret — "
            },
            {
              "text": "x x 5 6 5 x",
              "marks": ["code"]
            },
            {
              "text": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "d",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "The bass note, down one fret — "
            },
            {
              "text": "x x 4 5 5 x",
              "marks": ["code"]
            },
            {
              "text": "."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "answerId": "a",
      "explanation": [
        {
          "text": "In a second inversion the degrees run "
        },
        {
          "text": "5 1 3",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ", so the fifth is the bass note — and where the fifth sits depends only on the inversion, never on the string set. Augmented raises it a fret, which gives "
        },
        {
          "text": "x x 6 5 5 x",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ": "
        },
        {
          "text": "G#",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " "
        },
        {
          "text": "C",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " "
        },
        {
          "text": "E",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ". Diminished would drop the same note instead. The other three answers all move a voice that isn't the fifth."
        }
      ]
    },
